# Line endings must not depend on the tester's git config. core.autocrlf=true is
# the Windows default (and is set on this machine), so without a rule the same
# commit checks out with CRLF there and LF on Linux: markdown comparisons become
# platform-dependent, and a rebuild of the committed output under lib/ rewrites
# it back to LF, which leaves Windows contributors with phantom modifications in
# `git status` even though the bytes are identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored upstream tree is copied byte-for-byte and pinned by SHA-256 in
# vendor-manifest.json. Disable git's text conversion for it: with
# core.autocrlf=true a checkout rewrites LF to CRLF in the working tree, the
# recorded digests stop matching, and verify:vendor fails on any clone that is
# not configured exactly like the machine that vendored it. This rule must stay
# LAST: git uses the last matching pattern.
vendor/** -text
